Tata Motors Commercial Vehicles shares debut at 28% premium. Should investors stay on board?,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/tata-motors-commercial-vehicles-shares-debut-at-28-premium-should-investors-stay-on-board/articleshow/125264817.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:58:20 +0530","Tata Motors Commercial Vehicles Share Price: TMLCV shares opened at Rs 335 on the NSE, up 28.5% from the implied value of Rs 260.75, and at Rs 330.25 on the BSE, a 26.6% gain, reflecting solid investor appetite even as analysts expect near-term volatility."
Groww shares list at 14% premium over IPO price,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/groww-shares-list-at-14-premium-over-ipo-price/articleshow/125264762.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:58:15 +0530","Groww, India's largest investment platform, debuted on Dalal Street with a 14% premium, listing at Rs 114 and Rs 112 on BSE and NSE respectively. The Rs 6,632-crore IPO saw strong subscription, particularly from institutional investors. Analysts view Groww as a proxy for India's expanding financialization trend, recommending it as a medium-to-long-term investment opportunity."
"Infosys, TCS tumble up to 27% as IT meltdown drags Nifty vs global peers. Where's the heartbeat index headed?",https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/infosys-tcs-tumble-up-to-27-as-it-meltdown-drags-nifty-vs-global-peers-wheres-the-heartbeat-index-headed/articleshow/125264915.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:52:27 +0530","India's Nifty index shows modest one-year returns, lagging global peers. The IT sector, particularly Infosys and TCS, has dragged performance down. Financials, however, have been strong performers, delivering significant returns. Analysts anticipate a constructive outlook for Nifty over the next year, expecting stability and selective recovery in key sectors."
"Earnings growth to accelerate from Q3; banks, consumption &amp; defence among top bets: VK Vijayakumar",https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/expert-view/earnings-growth-to-accelerate-from-q3-banks-consumption-defence-among-top-bets-vk-vijayakumar/articleshow/125264822.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:51:26 +0530","India Inc’s earnings growth is set to accelerate sharply from Q3 FY26, led by banks, defence, and consumption sectors, says VK Vijayakumar, Chief Investment Strategist at Geojit. While FY26 growth is expected at 8–9%, FY27 could see double-digit expansion as domestic demand rises amid lower rates, tax cuts, and strong consumer spending."
Torrent Power shares in focus as Q2 PAT rises 50% YoY to Rs 742 crore,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/torrent-power-shares-in-focus-as-q2-pat-rises-50-yoy-to-rs-742-crore/articleshow/125264852.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:48:45 +0530","Torrent Power reported a significant 49.6% surge in profit after tax to Rs 742 crore for Q2 FY26, driven by a 9.8% revenue increase to Rs 7,876 crore. Improved merchant power sales and reduced finance costs bolstered performance. Despite higher depreciation, the company's strong quarterly results are expected to draw investor attention."
"Infosys, TCS, and other IT stocks in focus as Trump signals softer stance on H-1B visas",https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/infosys-tcs-and-other-it-stocks-in-focus-as-trump-signals-softer-stance-on-h-1b-visas/articleshow/125264796.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:46:25 +0530","U.S. President Donald Trump acknowledged the country’s need for skilled foreign workers, even as his administration moved to tighten visa regulations impacting global tech firms. In a Fox News interview, Trump was questioned about the future of H-1B visas and whether his administration planned to deprioritize them, according to Bloomberg."
Thermax shares in focus Q2 net profit tumbles 40% to Rs 119 crore; revenue down 5%,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/thermax-shares-in-focus-q2-net-profit-tumbles-40-to-rs-119-crore-revenue-down-5/articleshow/125264746.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:41:48 +0530","Thermax shares: The energy and environment solutions firm delivered a weak Q2 performance, with revenue down 5% year-on-year to Rs 2,474 crore and PAT plunging 40% to Rs 119 crore. PBT fell 35% to Rs 174 crore. Last year’s quarter had been boosted by a one-time Rs 66 crore incentive from the Maharashtra government under the PSI 2007 scheme."
Tata Motors is the worst-performing PV stock this year. Is it also the most undervalued to buy?,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/tata-motors-is-the-worst-performing-pv-stock-this-year-is-it-also-the-most-undervalued-to-buy/articleshow/125264707.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:39:44 +0530","Tata Motors has become the worst-performing passenger vehicle stock this year, sliding over 12% due to market share loss in EVs and struggles in its premium SUV portfolio. Despite global headwinds for JLR, analysts suggest the stock is undervalued, trading at a steep discount to peers, making it an attractive option for patient, long-term investors."
"Sensex rises 500 pts, Nifty tops 25,800 as U.S. trade hopes lift mood",https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/sensex-rises-350-pts-nifty-tops-25-750-as-u-s-trade-hopes-lift-mood/articleshow/125264535.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:35:40 +0530","Indian stocks surged on Wednesday, led by financials and IT, as optimism grew over a potential US trade deal and an end to the US government shutdown. The Sensex and Nifty both opened higher, reflecting boosted investor confidence in the market."
"HFCL, Premier Explosives stocks flash bullish signals, indicating possible uptrend",https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/hfcl-premier-explosives-stocks-flash-bullish-signals-indicating-possible-uptrend/slideshow/125264670.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:32:36 +0530","HFCL and Premier Explosives featured among stocks forming a bullish ‘White Marubozu’ pattern on November 11, signalling strong buying momentum and a potential uptrend."
Bajaj Finserv among 7 F&amp;O stocks with a sharp rise in futures open interest,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/bajaj-finserv-among-7-fo-stocks-with-a-sharp-rise-in-futures-open-interest/slideshow/125264587.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:27:41 +0530","A significant uptick in futures open interest signifies a substantial growth in the number of active, unexpired futures contracts in a specific security. This uptrend reflects an increasing number of participants either initiating new positions or expanding the size of their existing positions within the futures market."
Biocon shares in focus as company swings to Rs 84 crore profit in Q2,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/biocon-shares-in-focus-as-company-swings-to-rs-84-crore-profit-in-q2/articleshow/125264465.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:22:41 +0530","Biocon reported a strong turnaround in Q2FY26 with a net profit of Rs 84.5 crore against a loss of Rs 16 crore last year, driven by 21% YoY revenue growth to Rs 4,389 crore. Biosimilars led with 61% of revenue. The company also repaid key debts, aiming to boost margins and cut interest costs by FY27."
The Rs 1.5 lakh crore paradox: Why FIIs are dumping stocks but chasing IPOs,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/the-rs-1-5-lakh-crore-paradox-why-fiis-are-dumping-stocks-but-chasing-ipos/articleshow/125264420.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:19:42 +0530","Foreign institutional investors are divesting from Indian secondary markets while actively investing in IPOs, a trend termed 'The great divergence'. This split is driven by different investor types and a pursuit of valuation arbitrage, with long-term investors favoring primary markets for strategic entry points."
"Emmvee Photovoltaic Power IPO Day 2: Check GMP, subscription status. Should you apply?",https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/ipos/fpos/emmvee-photovoltaic-power-ipo-day-2-check-gmp-subscription-status-should-you-apply/articleshow/125264372.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:16:31 +0530","Emmvee Photovoltaic Power IPO: At a grey market premium (GMP) of Rs 5, or about 2.3% above the upper price band of Rs 217. This marks a decline from the earlier 9% premium, reflecting weaker investor sentiment toward the issue. At current levels, the stock is expected to list around Rs 222."
