RVNL shares drop 3% as PAT declines 20% YoY for Q2FY26,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/rvnl-shares-in-focus-as-pat-declines-20-yoy-for-q2fy26/articleshow/125264253.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:06:04 +0530","RVNL share price: Rail Vikas Nigam Ltd (RVNL) reported a 19.7% year-on-year decline in Q2FY26 profit after tax to Rs 230 crore, even as revenue rose 5.5% to Rs 5,123 crore. EBITDA fell 20% and margins narrowed, reflecting cost pressures amid moderate top-line growth."
SoftBank tanks 10% after $5.8-bn Nvidia stock sale,https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/softbank-tanks-10-after-5-8-bn-nvidia-stock-sale/articleshow/125264185.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:00:46 +0530","SoftBank has sold its entire stake in chip giant Nvidia for $5.8 billion. This move aims to generate cash for significant artificial intelligence investments. These include the ambitious US megaproject Stargate. SoftBank is a key investor in OpenAI, the creator of ChatGPT. The company reported a substantial profit increase in its latest quarter."
"Tata Power shares in focus as Q2 net profit jumps 14% to Rs 1,245 crore",https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/tata-power-shares-in-focus-as-q2-net-profit-jumps-14-to-rs-1245-crore/articleshow/125264178.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:00:26 +0530","Tata Power share price: Tata Power reported a 14% year-on-year rise in Q2FY26 net profit to Rs 1,245 crore, supported by higher operational revenue and improved EBITDA. However, net debt increased to Rs 54,000 crore due to elevated capital expenditure as the company continued investing in growth and infrastructure expansion."
"Profit booking and sideways markets hit equity flows, but SIPs stay steady: Suranjana Borthakur, Mirae Asset",https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/expert-view/profit-booking-and-sideways-markets-hit-equity-flows-but-sips-stay-steady-suranjana-borthakur-mirae-asset/articleshow/125248601.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:00:00 +0530","India’s mutual fund equity inflows fell 19% month-on-month, led by outflows in large-, mid-, and small-cap funds, said Suranjana Borthakur, Head of Distribution &amp; Strategic Alliances, Mirae Asset Investment Managers. However, SIP flows stayed strong above ₹29,500 crore, while investors shifted toward hybrid, passive, and gold funds amid market volatility, profit booking, and rising preference for diversified, stable investments."
"ETMarkets Smart Talk| Markets in fair value zone; time for singles, not boundaries: Manish Gunwani",https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/expert-view/etmarkets-smart-talk-markets-in-fair-value-zone-time-for-singles-not-boundaries-manish-gunwani/articleshow/125243398.cms,"Wed, 12 Nov 2025 09:00:00 +0530",Markets are in a fair value zone with supportive macro conditions. Near-term returns are expected to be moderate due to upcoming IPOs. Investors should focus on steady opportunities. Precious metals require reasonable allocation. Indian interest rates are trending lower. Earnings are neither great nor weak. Global credit spreads and AI capex pose risks.
